(6371417, 942922, 51747, '<td valign="top">Nice idea. The light is a bit harsh. I don''t know anything about studio lighting and I don''t know what to tell you to improve the shot. 5</td>', 'Nice idea. The light is a bit harsh. I don''t know anything about studio lighting and I don''t know what to tell you to improve the shot. 5', '2011-04-03 11:37:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371419, 942856, 51747, '<td valign="top">At first I just thought that this was a poor shot of a door with 13 ''images'' on it. The feet and legs were a real surprise and add a lot of interest.</td>', 'At first I just thought that this was a poor shot of a door with 13 ''images'' on it. The feet and legs were a real surprise and add a lot of interest.', '2011-04-03 11:43:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371420, 942538, 100393, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>This photo is clearly well executed and does a good job at meeting the challenge. However, I think it does lack depth and the intrinsic interest level of matches isn''t that high. I do like the way you''ve used  the border as a shelf though.<br/> <br/>Overall, there''s certainly nothing wrong with this image, I think you''ve made a fine job of it; it''s just that the final result doesn''t leave me with anything.<br/> <br/>It has to be said though, this isn''t the most inspiring challenge. In fact my average score given in this challenge is much less than 5.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. This photo is clearly well executed and does a good job at meeting the challenge. However, I think it does lack depth and the intrinsic interest level of matches isn''t that high. I do like the way you''ve used  the border as a shelf though. Overall, there''s certainly nothing wrong with this image, I think you''ve made a fine job of it; it''s just that the final result doesn''t leave me with anything. It has to be said though, this isn''t the most inspiring challenge. In fact my average score given in this challenge is much less than 5.', '2011-04-03 11:43:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371426, 943150, 100393, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>I''m not a fan of images of objects and as such you were always up against it for my vote. I am a fan of your lighting here though - I think that adds quite a lot more interest than there might have otherwise been. Looks like it could be a pre-digital radiology light box.<br/> <br/>In the end though - although this is a good idea, meets the challenge and is well executed, it isn''t beautiful as an image or intriguing or confounding in any way. Much of this is the fault of the challenge rather than your response to it, but nonetheless there''s little here to hold me.<br/> <br/>If it helps, my average score given for this challenge was quite a bit lower than the 5 I''ve dished out here.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. I''m not a fan of images of objects and as such you were always up against it for my vote. I am a fan of your lighting here though - I think that adds quite a lot more interest than there might have otherwise been. Looks like it could be a pre-digital radiology light box. In the end though - although this is a good idea, meets the challenge and is well executed, it isn''t beautiful as an image or intriguing or confounding in any way. Much of this is the fault of the challenge rather than your response to it, but nonetheless there''s little here to hold me. If it helps, my average score given for this challenge was quite a bit lower than the 5 I''ve dished out here.', '2011-04-03 11:50:31.000000', NULL, 1),
