(6372839, 942755, 1031, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.<br/> <br/>I made this grayscale because the colors were so far off due to the bad/mixed lighting in the pool hall, and the limitations of my ten year-old P&amp;S Olympus camera, working in Auto mode (see below).<br/> <br/>Resized original: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=944638" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_944638.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_944638.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_944638.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>It is (pleasantly) shocking to have gotten it so "nice and sharp" with a 1/20-second handheld exposure! :-)<br/> <br/>By the time I decided I was going to use this for my entry, it was too late to try and edit the colors individually, or to edit out the spots on the tabletop. However, I might not have done that anyway, since, with so many spots, it would be cutting it close to the line regarding removal of "distracting" elements ...</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I made this grayscale because the colors were so far off due to the bad/mixed lighting in the pool hall, and the limitations of my ten year-old P&S Olympus camera, working in Auto mode (see below). Resized original:   It is (pleasantly) shocking to have gotten it so "nice and sharp" with a 1/20-second handheld exposure! :-) By the time I decided I was going to use this for my entry, it was too late to try and edit the colors individually, or to edit out the spots on the tabletop. However, I might not have done that anyway, since, with so many spots, it would be cutting it close to the line regarding removal of "distracting" elements ...', '2011-04-04 14:18:17.000000', NULL, 0),
